-- Player-facing descriptions live beside the actual setting keys. Every
-- selectable setting has help; the menu wraps and scrolls the whole string.
local H={}
local HELP={
  adaptive_bosses='Off preserves existing story fights. Safe adapts native rival, Rocket boss, Elite Four, Champion and Gen 2 Red teams to earned badges and the encounter phase. Opening rivals stay short and low level. Rival starter continuity, native species and moves, and Boss level % apply. Chaos rolls 1-6 Pokemon without early strength or evolution limits. This overrides Trainers and Learnsets for these story fights only. Gym teams are controlled separately. Combat difficulty is not a beatability proof.',
  adaptive_gyms='Off keeps existing gym team behavior. Safe grows gym teams from 2 Pokemon at 0-1 badges to 6 at 5+ badges, with level-appropriate native evolutions, strength limits and simpler early moves. Chaos rolls 2-6 Pokemon without stage or early strength limits. Both keep the current leader\'s type theme (Blue uses mixed types), use earned badges for levels, and honor Boss level %. Gen 2 counts all 16 badges. This option controls gym species and moves instead of Trainers, BST limit and Learnsets; other battles still follow those settings. Native evolution families are used even with randomized evolution targets. Legendaries still obey their toggle. World progression safety is separate. High Boss percentages and Chaos teams can make early fights difficult.',

  gym_leaders='Shuffle the active game\'s native leaders, their teams and their original sprites. The gym location keeps its completion flag and TM reward. Safe caps moved teams to earned-badge progression and checks the shared world. Trainer Pokemon settings apply unless Adaptive teams is enabled. Chaos removes the world guarantee.',
  gym_entrances='Off keeps gym doors fixed. Safe shuffles paired gym entrances and proves all eight gyms, items, badges and the Champion remain reachable. Exits return to the entrance used. Chaos permits progression locks. Enabling this selects logical keys/HMs. All enabled world shuffles share the selected Safe or Chaos mode.',
  dungeon_entrances='Shuffle the audited entrances of Mt. Moon, Rock Tunnel, Digletts Cave, Seafoam, Victory Road, Pokemon Tower, Mansion, Power Plant, Silph Co. and Cerulean Cave. Internal floors stay native. Safe checks both sides, traversal HMs, story gates and paired returns. Forest, Safari, ship, Rocket Hideout, holes and teleport pads stay fixed. Chaos can create locks.',
  entrance_pool='Separate shuffles gyms with gyms and dungeons with dungeons. Mixed combines whichever of those two entrance options are enabled. Safe still validates the entire resulting route. A disabled entrance category never joins the pool.',
  badge_pairing='Independent uses the Gym badges setting separately from leader identity. With leader moves each leader with their native badge and selects a checked badge shuffle in Safe. Original gym completion flags and TM rewards stay with the location.',
  world_hints='Area gives broader locations; Exact adds the source check or entrance. Every four new rumors include one bogus roast. Re-reading a sign repeats its saved rumor. Paid hints can also be jokes. The progression tracker always reports factual requirements.',
  hidden_items='Off: keep vanilla hidden pickups, including the Gen 2 Machine Part. Safe: randomize native hidden items independently of visible field items, keeping required TMs and authored quest dependencies. Ordinary hidden spots cannot hold required keys/HMs unless their exact access is audited. Chaos: native items, TMs, keys and HMs may appear without a reachability guarantee. Pickup positions, Itemfinder behavior and collected flags stay native. Hidden coins stay vanilla. Existing saves keep their old shared field-item policy.',
  trainer_checks='Off: no trainer item drops. Safe: about 25% of distinct native trainer battles have a seeded item drop, drawn from native items and TMs. Keys and HMs can move to audited trainer wins; the validator checks access, badges, random starts and shuffled entrances. Assigned rewards are guaranteed on victory, so a required key cannot fail its roll. Chaos includes keys/HMs without reachability protection and can lock a run. First wins only; rematches cannot farm drops. Full bags send items to the PC. See the tracker reward log. All active world/item modes share Safe or Chaos.',

  wild_randomness={
    BALANCED='Balanced favors Pokemon with a similar base-stat total to the original encounter. Early routes usually have weaker or unevolved Pokemon, but there is no first-evolution-only rule. Choose Truly random for every native evolution stage from the start. This choice is separate from SAFE item/progression logic.',
    UNRESTRICTED='Truly random can select any permitted native Pokemon, including fully evolved Pokemon at low levels. It ignores the BST limit for wilds and never forces an evolution based on level. Legendaries follow their own toggle. SAFE still keeps a few required HM-learner slots; choose CHAOS safety to remove those protections. The encounter layout determines whether each area uses a small pool or individual slots.',
    LEGACY='This saved run keeps the encounter policy used by its older version. SAFE favored similar strength in variety/pool modes; full-slot and chaos pools used unrestricted choices. Existing encounter tables are preserved. New runs offer explicit Balanced and Truly random choices.',
  },
  area_encounters={
    VANILLA='Keep the cartridge species in each area. Wild level percentages still apply. Wild Pokemon balance and extra species do not randomize a vanilla encounter table.',
    HIGH_VARIETY='One stable replacement per native species in each area, plus Extra species. When extras are enabled, encounters draw from that saved area pool. A route does not contain the whole Pokedex; choose Slot by slot for more independent replacements. The Wild Pokemon choice controls strength matching.',
    AREA_POOL='Build a stable pool of 8 distinct Pokemon per area, plus Extra species. Encounters draw from that saved pool. Wild Pokemon chooses Balanced or Truly random. The pool and draw position survive saving and restarting.',
    CHAOS_POOL='An older 8-plus-extras area pool. New Balanced / Truly random settings control its strength matching; legacy saves keep their original unrestricted pool. This does not turn item logic into CHAOS.',
    FULL_SLOT_RANDOM='Replace each native encounter slot independently, using the Wild Pokemon balance setting. The results stay fixed for the seed. Identical species-and-level rows share a replacement in Gen 1. Extra species, if enabled, also adds the area pool. Set extras to 0 for only the slot replacements.',
  },
  wild_evolution={AS_ROLLED='Keep the exact species selected by the encounter table. A low-level fully evolved Pokemon is allowed when the selection policy permits it. No form is changed just because of encounter level. Evolution after capture uses your Evolution settings.',LEVEL='After choosing an encounter, promote it along its evolution chain when its level reaches a normal level-evolution threshold. Other evolution methods may promote at level 45. This does not change how captured Pokemon evolve. BST limits take priority; Truly random always keeps the rolled species.'},
  safety={SAFE='Check the supported HM, item, badge and start dependencies, protect essential rewards and provide usable starter attacks. This is progression protection, not a Pokemon strength setting. You can combine SAFE with Truly random wild Pokemon. The solver covers the authored world, not arbitrary added quests.',CHAOS='Disable progression guarantees. HMs, keys and badges can be placed behind their own requirements, and a run can become impossible. Pokemon balance is chosen separately. A CHAOS starting town is also a separate setting.'},
  random_start={OFF='Begin in the normal starting town. No portal will trigger after leaving the lab.',LOGIC='Choose one of the authored starting towns with checked escape requirements. Selecting this sets Progression safety to SAFE, enables logical key/HM placement and selects Safe badges. The portal happens once at the native intro handoff, not when you close setup.',CHAOS='Choose a starting town without a reachability guarantee. You may be stranded. This does not automatically change every item or Pokemon setting. The portal still waits for the native intro handoff.'},
  bst_match='BST means base-stat total: the sum of a species\' base stats. On enforces the chosen maximum difference for randomized starters, trainers, gifts, trades and balanced wilds. If nothing fits, the original species remains. Truly random wilds ignore this limit. Gen 1 uses five stats; Gen 2 uses six.',
  bst_difference='Set the maximum allowed base-stat-total difference, from 0 to 500. 50 gives roughly similar strength; 0 requires equal totals. This is a hard limit, not an evolution-stage filter. It applies only while BST limit is on; Truly random wilds are exempt.',
  base_stats='Unchanged keeps each Pokemon\'s native base stats. Shuffle redistributes its existing stat values among stats. Random generates a new distribution while preserving its total. Stats belong to the species, so the change affects both you and opponents.',
  types='Unchanged keeps native types. Evolution linked randomizes a family\'s types together. Random chooses types independently for each species. Only the active game\'s types are used: no Dark or Steel in Gen 1, and no Fairy in either generation.',
  evolutions='Unchanged keeps native evolution targets. Random changes what a Pokemon evolves into. The evolution method and requirements are handled separately by Trade evolutions. This does not restrict which stages can appear in the wild.',
  impossible_evos='On replaces trade-only or otherwise unsupported native evolution requirements with obtainable alternatives. Off keeps native requirements. This affects your Pokemon after capture, not the wild encounter pool.',
  starters='Unchanged keeps the normal starters. Random can choose any permitted native species. Two evolutions restricts starters to species with at least two remaining evolution stages. Only this setting has that stage restriction; it does not restrict wild encounters.',
  rival_starter='On makes the rival\'s corresponding starter follow the randomized starter mapping. Off leaves the rival\'s native starter choice. Other trainer Pokemon are controlled by Trainers.',
  movesets='Type bias guarantees at least one usable damaging same-type (STAB) attack in newly generated movesets at every level. It works in SAFE and CHAOS. Ordinary rolls have a 65% chance to use the matching-type pool, which can include status moves. It uses the Pokemon\'s current randomized types. This requires a suitable native attack: Gen 1 Dragon has none, since Dragon Rage deals fixed damage. Status, fixed-damage and sleep-dependent attacks do not satisfy the guarantee. Existing caught Pokemon keep their chosen moves. Unchanged keeps native learnsets; Random uses the native pool without type preference. Four-attack starter coverage runs automatically under Progression safety: SAFE; it has no separate toggle and preserves Type Bias STAB.',
  trainers='Unchanged keeps trainer species. Random selects from the permitted native roster. Similar strength favors a comparable base-stat total. Type themed selects around a shared type. The BST limit and legendary toggle still apply. Trainer levels are set separately.',
  trainer_levels='Adjust ordinary trainer levels from -50% to +50%. After a Logic Random Start portal, the zero-badge ceiling is level 9 before this modifier; each of the first eight earned badges adds 4 levels, and Kanto badges in Gen 2 add 5. The ceiling covers all maps, including interiors and side paths. Lower native teams stay lower. Walking, reloading and party levels never advance it. Bosses use their own setting.',
  boss_levels='Adjust Gym leaders, rivals and other recognized bosses from -50% to +50%. After a Logic Random Start portal, the zero-badge ceiling is level 12 before this modifier; each of the first eight earned badges adds 4 levels, and Gen 2 Kanto badges add 5. This overrides Trainer levels. Lower native teams stay lower; winning badges advances the ceiling.',
  wild_levels='Adjust wild levels from -50% to +50%. After a Logic Random Start portal, the zero-badge ceiling is level 7 before this modifier, usually giving level 5-7 encounters. Each of the first eight earned badges adds 4 levels; Gen 2 Kanto badges add 5. This covers side paths, interiors, fishing, fixed battles and Untamed encounters. Lower native levels stay lower. Party levels, map visits and restarting do not advance the ceiling. Species and evolution stage are separate choices.',
  trainer_ai='Normal uses the native AI policy. Strong enables the supported stronger move-selection policy for ordinary trainers. This does not change their species, moves or level settings.',
  boss_ai='Normal uses the native boss AI policy. Strong enables the supported stronger move-selection policy for recognized bosses. Pokemon and level settings are separate.',
  extra_species='Add 0-5 distinct species to the seeded area encounter pool. With extras on, encounters can draw from that pool as well as the native replacement mapping. 0 keeps only the base mapping/pool. Extras never add Pokemon from another generation.',
  statics='Control fixed encounters and gifted Pokemon. Unchanged keeps the original species. Random uses the permitted native pool; Similar strength favors comparable base-stat totals. This is separate from gifted items.',
  tms='Random changes the native moves taught by TMs. HMs always retain their native field moves. In new SAFE Gen 2 runs, the Rock Smash and Headbutt TMs also keep their native moves so those TM items still teach their original field moves. Rock Smash is not required for the native Morty story gate. TM/HM learning decides which Pokemon can learn the resulting moves.',
  tm_compat='Unchanged keeps native learnability except for SAFE protections. Type bias favors matching types. Random shuffles learnability. Full allows every native Pokemon to learn every native machine move. In new SAFE runs, original or randomized starters and their possible evolutions always remain HM learners, even with Keys + HMs off. You still need to obtain the HM, earn its badge and teach the move; no move or badge is granted by this setting.',
  field_items='Unchanged keeps pickups. Shuffle permutes eligible existing rewards. Random draws replacement items. Logical random uses the authored location/dependency solver for keys and HMs and selects SAFE progression safety. Chaos permits unchecked placements and selects CHAOS safety. You can switch back to Logical random at any time. With Random Start: Logic, this row cycles between Logical random and Chaos; turn Random Start off to choose an ordinary item mode. Switching to an ordinary mode keeps the current safety choice.',
  gift_items='Random includes supported ordinary NPC item gifts in item randomization. This is different from Pokemon gifts. Logical random and Chaos also place their supported key/HM rewards across NPC checks regardless of this ordinary-gift choice. Protected/missable story rewards stay fixed in SAFE. Managed one-time SAFE gifts use the PC with a notice when the bag is full.',
  progression_items='Safe shuffles supported keys and HMs with checked item, badge and story dependencies. Chaos shuffles without a completion guarantee. Choosing either also selects the matching Field items and Progression safety mode; they share one world plan. Off excludes keys/HMs and returns graph field modes to ordinary Random. Logic Random Start requires keys/HMs, so only Safe and Chaos are offered there; turn Random Start off to choose Off. Oak\'s Parcel, the Squirtbottle and escape-critical rewards stay fixed where needed in Safe. No HM is granted or taught automatically.',
  pc_item='Randomize the item stored in the bedroom PC at the start of a Gen 1 run. Gen 2 has no equivalent option here. This does not replace all items already stored in an existing save.',
  marts='Vanilla keeps shop inventory. Safe randomizes suitable ordinary stock. Chaos allows the broader supported shop pool. Mart safety is a separate switch that guarantees Pokeballs and Potions remain available.',
  mart_safety='Keep Pokeballs and Potions available in standard marts, including randomized shops, so catching and healing remain possible. A logical Saffron start also supplies Fresh Water for its native gate event.',
  trades='Unchanged keeps in-game NPC trades. Given randomizes the Pokemon received. Both also randomizes the requested Pokemon. This does not alter player-to-player link trades.',
  badges='Vanilla keeps Gym badge rewards. Safe keeps required badges reachable and shuffles the remaining valid choices, including with Random Start off. New logical item worlds check badges and items together. Chaos selects Chaos progression safety and can create locks. Logic Random Start requires Safe badges; turn Random Start off to choose other badge modes. Gen 2 shuffles Johto badges only; Kanto badges keep their native leaders.',
  allow_legendaries='Allow includes native legendary/mythical Pokemon in randomized pools. Block excludes them. Truly random still respects this toggle. Turning it on does not guarantee a legendary on every route.',
  seed_mode='Auto chooses a new seed for validation. Manual uses the number you enter, so the same game, settings and mod version can reproduce the run. A seed alone does not identify settings; the run code includes them.',
  manual_seed='Edit the seed one digit at a time. Left decreases a digit, right or A increases it. Select Save seed to accept; B discards this edit. Valid seeds are 1 through 2147483646.',
}
function H.describe(key,cfg,game,R)
  local value=HELP[key]
  if key=='mart_safety' and R.Gen1World and cfg.gym_leaders and R.Gen1World.enabled(cfg) and R.Gen1World.checked(cfg) then
    value='Safe world shuffles require Shop essentials On so catching and healing supplies cannot disappear. Choose Chaos or disable the world shuffles to make this optional.\n\n'..value
  end
  if game and game.data and game.data.gen2Encounters and key=='gym_entrances' then
    value='Off keeps gym doors fixed. Safe shuffles all 16 paired gym entrances, within Johto and Kanto separately, and checks items, badges and story progression through Red. Exits return to the entrance used. Chaos can cross regions and permit locks. Enabling this selects logical keys/HMs; enabled world shuffles share the selected Safe or Chaos mode.'
  end
  if game and game.data and game.data.gen2Encounters and key=='dungeon_entrances' then
    value='Gen 2: shuffle audited outer doors for Sprout Tower, Union Cave, Slowpoke Well, Burned Tower, Lighthouse, Ice Path, Dragon\'s Den, Tohjo Falls, Rock Tunnel, Diglett\'s Cave, Mt Moon and Mt Silver. Internal floors, ships, radio/rocket scripts and other dungeons stay native. Safe keeps Johto and Kanto entrance pools apart to protect native story events and checks progression through Red; Chaos can lock progression.'
  end
  if game and game.data and game.data.gen2Encounters and key=='badge_pairing' then value='Independent shuffles leaders separately from badges. With leader pairs each leader with their native badge. Johto and Kanto badges stay within their own regional pools, preserving the eight Johto badges required for field moves and the League.' end
  if game and game.data and game.data.gen2Encounters and key=='entrance_pool' then value='Separate keeps gyms and dungeons in different pools. Mixed combines the enabled categories. Safe always keeps Johto and Kanto apart so early Kanto badges cannot skip Johto story triggers. Chaos can mix across regions.' end
  if type(value)=='table' then value=value[cfg[key]] end
  if key=='random_start' and cfg.random_start~='OFF' then
    value=R.randomStartStatus(game,cfg)..'\n\n'..value
  end
  if key=='progression_items' and cfg.progression_items and cfg.field_items=='UNCHANGED' and cfg.gift_items=='UNCHANGED' then
    value='Keys/HMs are currently unchanged because both item channels are Unchanged. Select Safe or Chaos here to activate their shared world plan.\n\n'..value
  end
  return value or ('Change '..tostring(key):gsub('_',' ')..'.')
end
H.keys=HELP
return H
